<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">mount</ansi>

Your company can keep horses: one riding horse and one pack horse for
each member. A company of five can keep ten.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">The horses</ansi>

  <ansi fg="yellow">Pack horse</ansi> (120 gold)
  Carries 40 kg of the company's load, or 100 kg with a pack saddle.

  <ansi fg="yellow">Riding horse</ansi> (150 gold)
  Carries one member, once it wears a riding saddle; bare, it only
  carries 10 kg of load. A rider strains a quarter less with every step
  (<ansi fg="command">help strain</ansi>). The leader rides first, then companions in
  order. When every member rides, a route goes a tenth faster; if
  anyone walks, the company walks at their pace.

Horses are bought at a stable: the Dunmar West Gate, and the Trappers'
Post on the Old King's Road. Saddles are sold in the markets there.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Usage:</ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">mount</ansi>
  Your horses, their saddles, and what they add.

  <ansi fg="command">mount stable</ansi>
  At a stable: the horses for sale and their prices.

  <ansi fg="command">mount stable [type]</ansi>
  At a stable: buy a <ansi fg="command">pack-horse</ansi> or a <ansi fg="command">riding-horse</ansi>.

  <ansi fg="command">mount saddle [horse] [saddle]</ansi>
  Fit a saddle from your pack: a pack saddle on a pack horse, a riding
  saddle on a riding horse. Name the horse by number (<ansi fg="command">#2</ansi>) or kind
  (<ansi fg="command">pack</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">riding</ansi>). A saddle already fitted goes back into your pack.

  <ansi fg="command">mount unsaddle [horse]</ansi>
  Take a horse's saddle off, into your pack.

  <ansi fg="command">mount release [horse]</ansi>
  Let a horse go. Its saddle comes back to you; the gold doesn't.

If companions leave, you keep the horses you have, but can't buy more
of a kind until you're back under one per member.

See also: <ansi fg="command">help cargo</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help company inventory</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help strain</ansi>,
<ansi fg="command">help travel</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help company</ansi>.
